From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Mon, 22 Sep 2026 08:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] media: rkisp1: rk3568: use 34-bit DMA addresses

The rk3566/rk3568 ISP, like the i.MX8MP, addresses capture memory through
a 34-bit bus: the MI base-address registers hold bits [33:2] of the DMA
address (i.e. the address shifted right by two), and the ISP is wired
behind its own IOMMU.

Without RKISP1_FEATURE_DMA_34BIT the driver programmed the MI base
registers with the unshifted address and set only a 32-bit DMA mask, so
the memory interface issued a mistranslated write and the ISP IOMMU
faulted on the very first frame:

    rk_iommu fdff1a00.iommu: BUS_ERROR occurred at 0x0000000000000000

The ISP received and processed the frame (its interrupt fired) but no
buffer was ever written, so capture produced zero frames. Declare the
feature so the MI addresses are shifted and a 34-bit DMA mask is used,
which lets the rear OV5648 finally stream through the hardware ISP.

Upstream-Status: Pending

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
---
--- a/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rkisp1/rkisp1-dev.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rkisp1/rkisp1-dev.c
@@ -630,7 +630,8 @@
 	.features = RKISP1_FEATURE_MIPI_CSI2
 		  | RKISP1_FEATURE_SELF_PATH
 		  | RKISP1_FEATURE_DUAL_CROP
-		  | RKISP1_FEATURE_BLS,
+		  | RKISP1_FEATURE_BLS
+		  | RKISP1_FEATURE_DMA_34BIT,
 	.max_width = 3264,
 	.max_height = 2448,
 };
-- 
